`]}),e.jsx(x,{view:"ranks"}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Ranks, world size and process groups",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Distributed training runs one process per GPU, each with its own copy of the training script. The processes are numbered from 0 to N − 1, and a process's number is its rank. The number of processes in the run, N, is the world size. From here on, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"N"})," counts the ranks that take part in a collective, the whole world in the DDP and ZeRO examples, not parameters as in ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"6NT"}),"."]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The figure shows two nodes, each a server with eight GPUs. With one process per GPU, the world size is 16 and the ranks run from 0 to 15. A process's local rank is its GPU's place within its node, from 0 to 7. Rank 9 runs on the second GPU of Node 1, so its local rank is 1, the same as rank 1's on Node 0."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:'A process group is a set of ranks that communicate together. A run can hold several groups at once, and each communication step runs within one of them. The two highlight buttons outline the group shapes that tensor and data parallelism use. "One node" outlines ranks 0 to 7, the shape of a tensor-parallel group: it exchanges partial results in every layer, so it stays on the fast links inside one node. "Same local rank" outlines ranks 1 and 9, the shape of a data-parallel group when tensor parallelism fills each node, so its traffic crosses the network.'}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The launcher ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"torchrun"})," starts one process per GPU with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"--nproc-per-node=gpu"}),". Among the environment variables it sets for each process, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"RANK"})," holds its rank, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"LOCAL_RANK"})," its local rank and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"WORLD_SIZE"})," the number of processes in the job ",e.jsx(s,{id:"pytorch-torchrun",children:"PyTorch Contributors, 2026"}),"."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(a,{title:"Collectives say who holds what, before and after",accent:0,number:"9",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
