`,e.jsxs(t.li,{children:["Lane layout after Ovi ",e.jsx(s,{id:"ovi2026performance",children:"Ovi, 2026"})]}),`
`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Each layer is gathered, used and released",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["In fully sharded FSDP2, the parameters, gradients and optimizer state stay sharded on every rank outside each layer's computation. FSDP2 gathers and releases parameters by unit, a module whose parameters it treats together, and the diagram takes each layer as one unit. Before a layer's forward, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"GATHER WEIGHTS"})," all-gathers its full parameters, and after the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"FORWARD"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"RESHARD PARAMS"})," releases them. The backward runs from the last layer to the first. It gathers each layer's parameters again, computes its ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"BACKWARD"})," and reduce-scatters its gradients over the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"SYNC GRADS"})," connector. The ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"UPDATE"})," of the sharded state follows."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The two lanes stand for a sharding group of any size, and their collectives line up because each one synchronizes the group. The diagram leaves out prefetch, overlap, topology and failures. Its lane layout adapts Figure 2 of the first version of Ovi's paper, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"arXiv:2505.12832v1"}),", then titled ",e.jsx(t.em,{children:"A Study on Distributed Strategies for Deep Learning Applications in GPU Clusters"})," ",e.jsx(s,{id:"ovi2026performance",children:"Ovi, 2026"}),". The lifecycle itself comes from PyTorch FSDP ",e.jsx(s,{id:"zhao2023fsdp",children:"Zhao et al., 2023"}),". It is not Llama 3's, which keeps its parameters resident from forward until backward."]}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The stepper's ZeRO-3 mode runs the same lifecycle, but it gives each GPU whole groups of layers. FSDP2 shards every layer across all ranks and all-gathers each layer from all of them. Both send the same bytes."})]})]}),e.jsxs(a,{title:"ZeRO-2 and ZeRO-3 shard more state",accent:5,number:"23",items:"4",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"ZeRO-2: also shard gradients, still 1.0×"}),`
