`]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Full sharding sends 1.5 times DDP's bytes",children:[e.jsx(t.p,{children:"ZeRO-2 also shards the gradients. Each rank keeps only its reduce-scatter output, its shard of the reduced gradient. It runs ZeRO-1's two collectives, so in the idealized model it still sends 1.0 times DDP's bytes. The full parameters stay resident through forward and backward."}),e.jsx(t.p,{children:"ZeRO-3, full sharding, also shards the parameters. A layer's full parameters exist only while a computation needs them: an all-gather materializes them before the layer's forward and again before its backward, and a reduce-scatter leaves each rank its shard of the layer's gradients, as in the FSDP2 lanes."}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Count the bytes with P, the size of a full parameter or gradient buffer, under the ideal ring with N = 4. One reduce-scatter or all-gather over the whole model sends ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"P(N − 1)/N = 0.75P"})," per rank. DDP sends ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0.75P + 0.75P = 1.5P"})," per rank, or ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"6P"})," summed over the four ranks, and ZeRO-1 and ZeRO-2 send the same. Full sharding adds a second gather: the forward gathers, the backward gathers and the gradient reduce-scatters each send ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"0.75P"})," over all layers. That is ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"2.25P"})," per rank and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"9P"})," over the cluster, the end values of the stepper's ZeRO-3 count. The ratio to DDP is ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"2.25P / 1.5P = 1.5"}),". The extra half is the second all-gather of the parameters, the one that Llama 3 avoids by keeping its parameters resident until backward."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The 1.5× compares sent volume and says nothing about time. Prefetching a layer's parameters while another layer computes can hide part of the traffic ",e.jsx(s,{id:"zhao2023fsdp",children:"Zhao et al., 2023"}),". The time left exposed depends on the number of collectives, the topology, synchronization and overlap."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(a,{title:"ZeRO-1 is the first four-GPU strategy that fits 7B",accent:6,number:"24",children:[e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
